window.STUDY={"id":"ap-32-two-fields-agree-color","code":"AP-32","title":"Two fields agree → color","fig":"4.32","kicker":"Application · 32","lede":"A cyanotype contact print.","body":["Two ring gratings on film, one for carbon and one for silicon, were laid over the same sensitized sheet and exposed together: light reached the paper only where both films were clear, so Prussian blue is the agreement and nothing else. The two films are printed small on the left in their coset inks at the same scale; the beat and the blue share in the folio are computed from the two pitches, not quoted. Placeholder fields."],"source":"Made with the effect set: Cyanotype, Roller run-out, Paper tooth.","ref":{"w":1500,"h":1000},"variants":[{"id":"set","label":"As drawn","sw":[]}],"points":[],"colorHint":"The inks are dials of the effects: open Parameters and pick an effect.","paramsHint":"Every dial of the effects this piece uses.","spec":{"usage":{"id":"c-twofields","job":"concept","title":"Two fields agree → color","aspect":"3/2","uses":["fx-11-cyanotype","fx-02-ink-edge","fx-03-paper-tooth"]},"reference":{"grammar":"A cyanotype contact print. Two ring gratings on film, one for carbon and one for silicon, were laid over the same sensitized sheet and exposed together: light reached the paper only where both films were clear, so Prussian blue is the agreement and nothing else. The two films are printed small on the left in their coset inks at the same scale; the beat and the blue share in the folio are computed from the two pitches, not quoted. Placeholder fields."},"techniques":[{"id":"fx-11-cyanotype","name":"Cyanotype","short":"FX-11","atoms":["deposit","expose"],"params":{"dieSize":{"value":0.72,"range":[0.2,1],"label":"Motif size","step":0.01,"note":"motif height as a share of the plate"},"strokes":{"value":3,"range":[2,8],"label":"Brush strokes","step":1,"note":"strokes laid top to bottom, alternating direction"},"bAngle":{"value":-1.5,"range":[-30,30],"label":"Brush angle","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"tilt of the brush strokes"},"brushRag":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Brush-edge raggedness","step":0.01,"note":"how far bristles and drag push each stroke edge in and out"},"uneven":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Coating unevenness","step":0.01,"note":"streaks and drag in the sensitizer thickness"},"dry":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Dry-brush tails","step":0.01,"note":"how far the load runs out before the brush lifts: bristle streaks on the tooth peaks"},"pool":{"value":0.25,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pooling","step":0.01,"note":"sensitizer beading where the brush lands and stops, and the drying rim along each edge"},"expo":{"value":1.35,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Exposure","step":0.01,"note":"sun dose; 1 = full development of an unshaded coat"},"lift":{"value":0,"range":[0,24],"label":"Object lift","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"height of the lifted parts above the sheet. It sets the penumbra width and its offset away from the sheet light"},"contact":{"value":1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Contact","step":0.01,"note":"share of the subject pressed flat (sharp); the rest curls up (soft)"},"scatter":{"value":0.1,"range":[0.05,1],"label":"Sky scatter","step":0.01,"note":"penumbra per px of lift: skylight and haze around the sun"},"trans":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Translucency","step":0.005,"note":"UV passing through leaf tissue (cut card: 0)"},"bleed":{"value":0.06,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wash bleed","step":0.01,"note":"Prussian blue carried downhill into the whites during the wash, in streaks"},"density":{"value":1.45,"range":[0.3,2],"label":"Film density","step":0.01,"note":"film density of a fully exposed coat (Beer–Lambert: deeper and more saturated)"},"cL":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Custom tone · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"cC":{"value":0.12,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Custom tone · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ch":{"value":256,"range":[0,360],"label":"Custom tone · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"seed":{"value":33,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Coating = brush strokes in stroke space (along s, across t): a load that runs out along the stroke; edges displaced by per-side noise (raggedness); a set-down pool and a drying rim; bristle streaks × the stock height decide where a dry brush still deposits. Thickness τ = load × unevenness (streaks + low-frequency drag) + pools; overlapping strokes add (a double coat prints deeper); paper valleys hold more sensitizer. Objects (procedural fern frond, grass with spikelets, or a cut-card motif) are an AA clip. Lift = a smooth field × the lift dial; contact sets how much lies flat. Shadow: for each lift level z the clip is sampled toward the sheet light at z · cot(elevation) (smeared ±20 % along the light) and blurred by z × sky scatter; each pixel blends the two levels around its lift. Exposure E = 1 − shadow × (1 − translucency). Develop: r = ((1 − e^(−2.2·exposure·E)) ÷ (1 − e^(−2.2)))^1.35, capped at 1.2; the coat saturates as τ' = 1.3·(1 − e^(−τ/1.3)); density = τ' × (a faint stain + r) × film density. Overexposure fills the penumbra in. Wash: unexposed coating rinses away; Prussian blue bleeds a little downhill into the whites, in streaks. Color = Beer–Lambert film of the tone (fresh, classic, peroxide-oxidized, tea-toned). Light last: × the stock's shading under the sheet light.","limits":"object lift > 18 px: penumbra wider than the leaflets: the fern dissolves into a cloud. exposure > 2.5: penumbra fills in; fine pinnules and awns vanish. exposure < .5: pale, greenish print: reads as underexposed. raggedness > .8: stroke edges tear into islands. strokes > 6: brush marks shrink into stripes"},{"id":"fx-02-ink-edge","name":"Roller run-out","short":"FX-02","atoms":["deposit"],"params":{"streak":{"value":1.25,"range":[1,10],"label":"Streak","step":0.1,"note":"film-split clumps stretched along the stroke: a dry roller, a dragged brush"},"pressure":{"value":1,"range":[0.4,1],"label":"Roller pressure","step":0.01,"note":"pressure in the solid; below 1 the body starts to open up"},"angle":{"value":0,"range":[0,360],"label":"Stroke angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"direction the roller travels (it runs out along this vector)"},"edge":{"value":1.7,"range":[0,1.7],"label":"Edge position","step":0.005,"note":"where the run-out is centered across the plate"},"width":{"value":4,"range":[1,420],"label":"Transition","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"width of the run-out band"},"wAmp":{"value":18,"range":[0,90],"label":"Edge warp","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far the edge line wanders"},"wScale":{"value":90,"range":[8,400],"label":"Warp scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander"},"wOct":{"value":3,"range":[1,5],"label":"Warp octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"detail in the wander"},"bite":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock bite","step":0.01,"note":"how much the stock height (vs film-splitting noise) decides where ink lands"},"breakup":{"value":1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Break-up ↔ thin","step":0.01,"note":"1 = ink film breaks into marks on the peaks as pressure falls; 0 = the film stays whole and thins to tone"},"starve":{"value":0.004,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"the lowest share of the surface never takes ink. Pinholes in the solid, placed by the paper's valleys and pits"},"wick":{"value":0.03,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried along fibers into the run-out (hairline feathering)"},"mottle":{"value":0.05,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation (its low-frequency cloudiness) varying the film thickness"},"split":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,10],"label":"Film split","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"clump size of the film-splitting noise (the roller's own speckle)"},"iL":{"value":0.18,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"iC":{"value":0.005,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ih":{"value":280,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure (Beer–Lambert: thicker = deeper, more saturated)"},"mInset":{"value":14,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":60,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":14,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"mBite":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":9,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Pressure = dropoff curve of the signed distance to a warped edge line (stroke direction, transition width), × the mask. Ink chain: the stock height under the inked area (blended with film-splitting noise, clumped and streaked along the stroke) is ranked to percentiles; pressure P inks exactly the top P of the surface, peaks first. Starve: valleys below the threshold never take ink. Wick: fibers carry ink past the edge. Mottle: paper formation thins the film. Film thickness thins with pressure unless the film breaks up; color = Beer–Lambert film in linear light. Light last: × the stock's shading. The ink sits in the tooth, not on top of it.","limits":"transition < 4 px: reads as a hard vector edge: no run-out to see. break-up < .3: the edge becomes a gradient: the \"AI gradient\" failure. stock bite < .3: speckle stops following the paper and reads as digital dither. streak > 6: marks read as scanlines unless the angle is off-axis"},{"id":"fx-03-paper-tooth","name":"Paper tooth","short":"FX-03","atoms":["form"],"params":{"scale":{"value":4,"range":[0.5,24],"label":"Tooth scale","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"feature size of the tooth (noise wavelength), not a tile zoom"},"oct":{"value":4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"layers of finer detail"},"fibers":{"value":2.4,"range":[0,40],"label":"Fibers","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"laid fibers per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"fLen":{"value":14,"range":[2,80],"label":"Fiber length","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber length"},"fWidth":{"value":0.4,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Fiber width","step":0.02,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber width"},"pits":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,40],"label":"Pits","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"depressions per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"pers":{"value":0.42,"range":[0.15,0.85],"label":"Persistence","step":0.01,"note":"amplitude kept per octave: the spectral dropoff of the tooth"},"aniso":{"value":1.4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Anisotropy","step":0.05,"note":"tooth stretched along the grain angle. Machine-made paper is never isotropic; 1 = the 1999 \"paper\" filter look"},"form":{"value":0.25,"range":[0,1],"label":"Formation","step":0.01,"note":"low-frequency cloudiness of the sheet (fiber flocs); also mottles any ink printed on it"},"formScale":{"value":60,"range":[10,200],"label":"Formation scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"size of the flocs"},"fAngle":{"value":6,"range":[0,180],"label":"Grain angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"machine direction of the fibers and the tooth"},"fSpread":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Grain spread","step":0.01,"note":"0 = all fibers on the grain; 1 = any direction"},"depth":{"value":0.05,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Relief","step":0.005,"unit":"px","note":"height of the tooth in CSS px: how hard the light can rake it. The slider is weighted to the subtle end."},"diffuse":{"value":0.55,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"fRaise":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fiber raise","step":0.01,"note":"how far fibers stand proud of the sheet"},"pDepth":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pit depth","step":0.01,"note":"how deep pits go"},"paperL":{"value":0.968,"range":[0.85,1],"label":"Paper L","step":0.001,"note":"OKLab lightness of the stock under the sheet light. Below 1 so lit walls, foil and sheen have headroom to brighten; 1 = the white of the page (highlights clip)"},"fDark":{"value":0.014,"range":[0,0.15],"label":"Fiber tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening of fibers"},"pDark":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Pit tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening in pits"},"tL":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"tC":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Fill tint · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"th":{"value":250,"range":[0,360],"label":"Fill tint · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"tAmt":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint amount","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ambient fill takes the tint (shadows go cool / warm)"},"mInset":{"value":22,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":2.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":28,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"lift":{"value":1,"range":[0,4],"label":"Sheet lift","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"thickness / curl of the sheet: sizes its shadow on the page"},"mBite":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":21,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Height = fbm at the tooth scale (octaves, persistence = how fast detail drops off), reshaped by the distribution curve; blended with low-frequency formation. Fibers: curved capsules at a count per 100 × 100 CSS px near the grain angle, raised into the height; pits: small depressions. Both also darken the albedo slightly. Normal from the height gradient → Lambert under the sheet light (azimuth + elevation from the light puck). Diffuse share vs ambient fill; the fill can be tinted. The same field is the stock for FX-01 and FX-02: its peaks take ink first, its valleys starve, its fibers wick. Mask = the sheet's cut or deckle edge; the sheet casts a contact + ambient shadow onto the page by the same light.","limits":"relief > .6 px: reads as stucco: the stock-filter emboss look. anisotropy < 1.3: isotropic tooth reads as a 1999 paper filter. tooth scale < .8 px: collapses into per-pixel noise: digital grain. fibers > 30 /100×100 px: felt, not paper. light elevation < 15°: every fiber becomes a hard ridge; ok for a raking-light study, not for a page"}],"pass_order":["Cyanotype · A sun print.","Roller run-out · A solid that runs out.","Paper tooth · White stock that is not a screen."]}};
